  "notes": [
    "All fifteen services now evaluate on both critical environments, plus demo-orders retaining Test and Dev for its bounded probe. Thirty-two evaluators.",
    "Measured rather than assumed: containers average 40.6 MiB and Docker has 31 GiB allocated, so thirty-two is about four per cent of available memory at effectively no CPU, since each container works around 1.5 seconds per five-minute cycle.",
    "Connections remain the real budget and stay comfortable: thirty-one batch evaluators at a measured 0.27 per cent duty cycle plus one sustained probe projects to roughly 1.1 against a ceiling of 5.",
    "This is what gives demo-sms-notifications, demo-subscription-pause, demo-support-assistant and demo-fraud-screening their first evaluations, so all 24 flags finally have a caller."
  ]
